This directory (src/tokenizer/vendor/llamacpp_unicode/) contains source vendored, with only the
change noted below, from:

  Project: llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

  Files copied verbatim from a local checkout of the ROCmFPX fork of llama.cpp
  (C:\Users\user\dev\ROCmFPX, itself MIT-licensed: "Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors;
  Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Carlo Pasquale (Charlie12345), ROCmFPX additions"):

    src/unicode.h       -> unicode.h
    src/unicode.cpp     -> unicode.cpp
    src/unicode-data.h  -> unicode-data.h
    src/unicode-data.cpp -> unicode-data.cpp

  These four files are llama.cpp's Unicode codepoint-classification tables and its hand-written
  (regex-engine-free) pre-tokenizer splitters, including `unicode_regex_split_custom_qwen35`,
  which implements byte-for-byte the exact pre-tokenizer regex Qwen3.8-27B's tokenizer.json
  specifies:

    (?i:'s|'t|'re|'ve|'m|'ll|'d)|[^\r\n\p{L}\p{N}]?[\p{L}\p{M}]+|\p{N}| ?[^\s\p{L}\p{M}\p{N}]+[\r\n]*|\s*[\r\n]+|\s+(?!\S)|\s+

  r4dx's own src/tokenizer/bpe_tokenizer.cpp calls `unicode_regex_split()` (unicode.cpp) to
  pre-tokenize, and separately ports (does not vendor verbatim -- see the comment atop
  bpe_tokenizer.cpp) the BPE merge loop from llama.cpp's `llm_tokenizer_bpe_session::tokenize()`
  and `tokenizer_st_partition()` (src/llama-vocab.cpp in the same ROCmFPX checkout), adapted to
  r4dx's own vocab/merge-rank data structures loaded from tokenizer.json.

